Changing the type of `num_vec` from `u32` to `int` allows it to correctly represent negative values returned by `pci_msix_vec_count()`. This ensures that if an error occurs (indicated by a negative return value), the condition `num_vec <= 0` will evaluate to true, allowing for proper error handling in the subsequent logic.

